  "observations": [
    "Eligible knot groups are processed in descending order and reduced atomically to simple knots. The range minimum selects eligible groups; it does not specify their resulting multiplicity. Degree-one groups disappear.",
    "Every accepted bounded proposal is certified against the complete original source in normalized parameter correspondence. Per-edit errors cannot accumulate. Some(0) in Rust is strict; None explicitly permits unrestricted removal.",
    "The captured SDK removes three interior vertices from a degree-one polyline even at 1e-9. One original vertex lies more than three units from the resulting endpoint segment. Six positive-tolerance records therefore retain conservative bounded results instead of copying unsafe SDK edits.",
    "A single-knot API can reduce a fresh fitted cubic join from multiplicity three to two with a certified 1e-6 bound while declining a forced simple-knot basis at that tolerance. This does not establish the adaptive Loft Refit subdivision or polishing policy.",
    "Periodic curves fail explicitly. Bounded proposals require degree <=16 and nonzero common-sign weights. More than 256 eligible groups fail before editing. Existing certificate work and bit limits remain in force.",
    "Constant stored coordinate and weight channels are restored after basis interpolation and before certification, including negative common weight gauges. The native adapter uses usd-brep for basis proposals and shares portable selection and certification."
  ],
